Follow the Mobile Engineering Playbook as the shared baseline:

https://github.com/sergii/mobile-engineering-playbook

When the playbook is available in context or the workspace, read:

- `MOBILE_ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md`
- `guides/decision-ladder.md`
- `guides/agent-failure-modes.md`
- `guides/platform-native-rules.md`
- any archetype explicitly selected for this product

Product-specific documented rules override generic examples. Do not silently select an archetype.

Default behavior:

- build thin vertical slices before broad infrastructure;
- prefer React Native and Expo primitives;
- start with `StyleSheet`;
- keep TypeScript strict;
- add dependencies only when they solve demonstrated problems;
- determine CNG/native-project ownership before editing `ios/` or `android/`;
- prefer Expo Router Protected Routes for route-level auth/authorization;
- verify meaningful UI and native behavior in the running mobile runtime;
- use the playbook's decision ladder before adding cross-cutting tools.

Keep project-specific domain rules local to the product repository instead of duplicating the shared playbook here.
